    "TRAP-PREREGISTRATION.md": {
      "hash": "c48db2fa80e8",
      "indexed_at": "2026-08-11T15:58:06.864558+00:00",
      "language": "markdown",
      "lines": 168,
      "mtime_ns": 1786310602072948200,
      "size": 7337,
      "symbols": [
        {
          "docstring": "Whether the routed arm falls for a **trap** less often than the unrouted arm, where a trap is an item whose obvious method yields a specific wrong ans",
          "lines": [
            12,
            23
          ],
          "name": "What is being tested",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "- Generator: `bench/trap-prompts.js`, output `bench/trap-candidates.jsonl`. - **n = 60**, from a pool of 71 traps; **76 non-trap items were refused**",
          "lines": [
            24,
            37
          ],
          "name": "Corpus",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "| arm | meaning | |---|---| | `a` | unrouted \u2014 RoT MoE hooks disarmed | | `b` | routed \u2014 the shipped nine-lens router active |",
          "lines": [
            38,
            46
          ],
          "name": "Arms",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "For each item, the arm's answer is parsed as the first integer in its reply.",
          "lines": [
            47,
            60
          ],
          "name": "Outcome classification, fixed now",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "McNemar exact (two-sided binomial, p = 0.5) on the **discordant pairs** of `CORRECT`. \u03b1 = 0.05.",
          "lines": [
            61,
            65
          ],
          "name": "Primary test",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "The informative band is the count of discordant pairs (`RotTrap.band`). **If band < 10 the result is reported as `noPower`** (`RotCeiling.noPower`) \u2014",
          "lines": [
            66,
            73
          ],
          "name": "Power floor, fixed now",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "Both controls that killed earlier corpora are applied from the start, not bolted on when a headline looks good:",
          "lines": [
            74,
            90
          ],
          "name": "Deconfounding, fixed now",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "| condition | verdict | |---|---| | band < 10 | `noPower` \u2014 corpus cannot decide | | band \u2265 10, deconfounded p \u2265 0.05 | `null` \u2014 no advantage establis",
          "lines": [
            91,
            101
          ],
          "name": "Decision rule, fixed now",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "It would mean: on mechanically-checkable questions of this repository where the obvious method is wrong, the routed arm is measurably less likely to g",
          "lines": [
            102,
            118
          ],
          "name": "What a win here would and would not mean",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "Measured in rep 1: band 12, **all 12 discordant pairs to the unrouted arm**, p = 0.0005. The table maps that to `null`, because `advantage` requires t",
          "lines": [
            119,
            142
          ],
          "name": "A1.1 The decision table had no row for a routed LOSS",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "The first scoring run gave **0 correct out of 60 for both arms**. The arms were right; `firstInt` rejected any digit followed by a period, so `**0.**`",
          "lines": [
            143,
            159
          ],
          "name": "A1.2 The answer parser was defective in rep 1 and was repaired mid-analysis",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "Rep 1 is a single pass per arm. The calibration corpus needed two reps before its band was trustworthy. Rep 2 is required before this is treated as a",
          "lines": [
            160,
            169
          ],
          "name": "A1.3 Reproducibility is not yet established",
          "type": "section"
        }
      ]
    },
